  "content": [
    {
      "id": "content",
      "title": "Content",
      "icon": "box",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "<strong>11:57 PM in Bengaluru</strong>.<br>The Flipkart war room feels like a launchpad. Dashboards glow in the dim light traffic per second, inventory count",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "ers, Kafka lags, CPU &amp; memory graphs. Some lines are green, a few turn amber, one or two flirt with red.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Thanks for reading Alex’s Substack! Subscribe for free to receive new posts and support my work.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Coffee cups clutter the table. Engineers sit quietly, not coding anymore. Code freeze happened days ago. Tonight is not about writing code, it’s about watching systems&nbsp;<em>perform</em>.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Someone whispers:&nbsp;<em>“T-minus 3 minutes.”</em>",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "At exactly&nbsp;<strong>12:00:00</strong>, the Flipkart banner flips to&nbsp;<strong>Big Billion Sale</strong>. Push notifications blast across India.&nbsp;<strong>Crores of taps per second</strong>&nbsp;slam into the system.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "And somewhere in Pune,&nbsp;<strong>Alex taps “Buy Now.”</strong><br>This is the story of what happens next.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "<strong>The Mall in the Cloud</strong>",
          "content": "<strong>The Mall in the Cloud</strong>",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "“Imagine Flipkart as a giant mall, but it exists in the cloud.”",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<strong>CDN (Content Delivery Network)</strong>&nbsp;→ Like billboards all over India. Instead of fetching banners and scripts from Bengaluru, you read them from a server near your house. That’s why the homepage loads instantly.",
            "<strong>WAF (Web Application Firewall) + API Gateway</strong>&nbsp;→ Like the mall’s main gate and security guards. They filter bots, block abusive traffic, and decide if Alex’s request is legitimate.",
            "<strong>Load Balancers</strong>&nbsp;→ The traffic cops. A global LB sends Alex to the nearest regional data center (Mumbai, Chennai, Delhi). Then a regional LB routes him to a healthy server pod.",
            "<strong>Microservices</strong>&nbsp;→ Inside the mall, each shop does one job: catalog, cart, payments, inventory, orders, notifications. They run inside Kubernetes, wrapped in a service mesh so they can talk securely.",
            "<strong>Kafka</strong>&nbsp;→ The conveyor belt between shops. Instead of yelling, services drop messages on Kafka and others pick them up at their own pace.",
            "<strong>Databases</strong>&nbsp;→ Stockrooms. Strict vaults (MySQL/Postgres) for money; wide bins (Cassandra/ElasticSearch) for catalog and search; fast drawers (Redis) for ultra-hot data like carts and stock.",
            "<strong>Observability</strong>&nbsp;→ CCTV everywhere: Prometheus for metrics, Grafana dashboards, ELK logs, tracing. If one corridor jams, alerts ring instantly."
          ],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": [],
          "ordered": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "<strong>Alex’s Midnight Order, The Flow</strong>",
          "content": "<strong>Alex’s Midnight Order, The Flow</strong>",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Let’s trace Alex’s iPhone order in real-time.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "<strong>1. Homepage</strong>",
          "content": "<strong>1. Homepage</strong>",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "When Alex opens the app:",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<strong>80% of the load</strong>&nbsp;is served by&nbsp;<strong>CDNs</strong>: banners, images, JS.",
            "Dynamic API calls go through the&nbsp;<strong>API Gateway</strong>, where a&nbsp;<strong>rate limiter</strong>ensures one user/device/IP doesn’t flood the system. Suspicious ones get challenged.",
            "<strong>Feature flags</strong>&nbsp;(simple config switches) decide if Alex sees an experimental banner or a bank-specific promo."
          ],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": [],
          "ordered": false
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The secret: by handling most stuff at the&nbsp;<strong>edge</strong>, core servers are shielded.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "<strong>2. Search</strong>",
          "content": "<strong>2. Search</strong>",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Alex types&nbsp;<strong>“iPhone 15 Pro.”</strong>",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "The query hits the&nbsp;<strong>Search microservice</strong>, backed by&nbsp;<strong>ElasticSearch</strong>. Optimized indexes return results in ~50 ms.",
            "Each result needs prices/promos. Instead of hitting MySQL every time, the&nbsp;<strong>Pricing service</strong>&nbsp;pulls from&nbsp;<strong>Redis</strong>(periodically synced with MySQL)."
          ],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": [],
          "ordered": false
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Why not just MySQL? Because at this scale, even reading 10 million rows/sec would melt it. Redis handles micro-updates and insane read volume.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "<strong>3. Product Page</strong>",
          "content": "<strong>3. Product Page</strong>",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Alex taps the iPhone listing.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<strong>Catalog service</strong>&nbsp;fetches structured product details from&nbsp;<strong>Cassandra + ElasticSearch</strong>.",
            "<strong>Inventory service</strong>&nbsp;checks&nbsp;<strong>Redis</strong>&nbsp;for stock count.",
            "That little line&nbsp;<em>“Only 3 left in stock”&nbsp;</em>is not fake. It’s updated in near real-time by&nbsp;<strong>Kafka events</strong>&nbsp;flowing from warehouse DBs."
          ],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": [],
          "ordered": false
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "This separation (catalog vs. inventory) avoids bottlenecks. Catalog = descriptive data (read-heavy). Inventory = small, hot, transactional counters.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "<strong>4. Add to Cart</strong>",
          "content": "<strong>4. Add to Cart</strong>",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Alex adds the iPhone to his cart.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<strong>Redis</strong>&nbsp;is updated immediately (primary source for speed).",
            "An&nbsp;<strong>async background write</strong>&nbsp;persists the cart in&nbsp;<strong>Cassandra</strong>&nbsp;for durability."
          ],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": [],
          "ordered": false
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Why this hybrid? Redis alone is too risky (data lost if memory crashes). Cassandra ensures persistence without slowing the hot path.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "<strong>5. Checkout</strong>",
          "content": "<strong>5. Checkout</strong>",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The&nbsp;<strong>Order Orchestrator</strong>&nbsp;takes charge. Think of it as a conductor ensuring the orchestra plays in sync:",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Calls&nbsp;<strong>Inventory</strong>&nbsp;to reserve the item.",
            "Confirms&nbsp;<strong>address &amp; delivery slot</strong>.",
            "Passes to&nbsp;<strong>Payment Orchestrator</strong>."
          ],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": [],
          "ordered": true
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Every microservice call is logged with a correlation ID. If something goes wrong, engineers can trace Alex’s journey across dozens of services.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "<strong>6. Reservation</strong>",
          "content": "<strong>6. Reservation</strong>",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "This is the heart of the system. Here’s how Flipkart avoids overselling:",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Acquire a&nbsp;<strong>distributed lock</strong>&nbsp;(via Redis/ZooKeeper) on the iPhone SKU.",
            "Check the&nbsp;<strong>stock counter</strong>&nbsp;in Redis.",
            "If enough units exist → decrement atomically.",
            "Create a&nbsp;<strong>reservation TTL (5 minutes)</strong>&nbsp;→ Alex has this time to finish payment.",
            "Kafka event informs other systems: “Item reserved.”",
            "Release the lock."
          ],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": [],
          "ordered": false
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "If Alex fails to pay, stock auto-releases when TTL expires. That’s why 1000 iPhones don’t become 2000 oversold orders.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "<strong>7. Payments</strong>",
          "content": "<strong>7. Payments</strong>",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Payments are unpredictable. Banks can be slow. Gateways can timeout.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The&nbsp;<strong>Payment Orchestrator</strong>&nbsp;is built for this:",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Generates an&nbsp;<strong>idempotency key</strong>&nbsp;so retries don’t double-charge.",
            "Chooses the best route (UPI/Card/Wallet) based on live success scores.",
            "Sets&nbsp;<strong>hard timeouts</strong>&nbsp;(e.g., UPI = 15 sec). If slow, retries on another gateway.",
            "Every transaction is logged in an&nbsp;<strong>append-only ledger DB</strong>&nbsp;→ audit-proof, tamper-proof."
          ],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": [],
          "ordered": false
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "To Alex, this feels like:&nbsp;<em>“Processing your payment…”</em>&nbsp;even though in the backend, multiple retries and failovers may be happening.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "<strong>8. Order Commit</strong>",
          "content": "<strong>8. Order Commit</strong>",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "If payment succeeds:",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<strong>Order service</strong>&nbsp;writes the final record into&nbsp;<strong>MySQL/Postgres (ACID-safe)</strong>.",
            "Kafka events trigger:",
            "Notifications (SMS, email, push).",
            "Ekart logistics (nearest warehouse starts packing)."
          ],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": [],
          "ordered": false
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "If payment fails? Alex sees a clear message not silence:",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<em>“Processing…”</em>&nbsp;if bank callback is late.",
            "<em>“Payment failed, stock restored.”</em>&nbsp;if reservation expires."
          ],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": [],
          "ordered": false
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Predictable, honest UX &gt; Silent failure.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "<strong>Flash Sale Mechanics</strong>",
          "content": "<strong>Flash Sale Mechanics</strong>",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "n a flash sale, lakhs of people hit&nbsp;<em>“Buy Now”</em>&nbsp;at the&nbsp;<strong>same second</strong>. Without guardrails, servers crash, stock oversells, and nobody is happy.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "To stop this chaos, Flipkart uses five key tricks that work together.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "First comes the&nbsp;<strong>token bucket at the gateway</strong>. Think of it like giving every user a handful of tokens maybe 10 per second.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Every time you send a request (like add to cart or check stock), you spend a token. If you run out, you wait.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "This stops a single user or bot from hammering the system with thousands of requests while still letting normal customers through smoothly.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Next is the&nbsp;<strong>waiting room (pre-queue)</strong>. Imagine a stadium with only a few gates. If everyone pushes in at once, it’s chaos. Instead, the crowd waits outside, and security lets people in small waves.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That’s what happens here. You may see a “You’re in line” message for a few seconds, while the backend processes earlier requests. This way the system doesn’t collapse under sudden spikes, and users feel things are fair.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Now, the&nbsp;<strong>hot key problem</strong>. In Redis (or any cache), each product has a counter. During a flash sale, one product say the iPhone is requested millions of times.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That counter becomes a “hotspot” and one Redis server can melt under the load. The fix is&nbsp;<strong>sharding</strong>: split that iPhone counter into multiple smaller counters (like sku:iphone:a, sku:iphone:b…).",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Updates spread across servers, and the system aggregates them when showing stock. This spreads the heat.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Another big issue is the&nbsp;<strong>cache stampede</strong>. Suppose a cache key (like the stock count) expires. Suddenly, thousands of requests rush to refresh it from the database at the same time, and the DB collapses.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The trick is&nbsp;<strong>single-flight refresh</strong>: the first request refreshes the data, and others just wait for that result instead of all hitting the DB.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Add in randomized expiries (jitter) so not everything expires together, and the system stays safe.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Finally,&nbsp;<strong>reservation TTLs</strong>&nbsp;keep things fair.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "When Alex clicks&nbsp;<em>Buy Now</em>, the system reserves the item for him but only for a limited time (say 5 minutes). If payment succeeds, the item is his.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "If he quits or fails to pay, the timer expires and the stock goes back into the pool. This prevents people from hoarding stock forever without completing the purchase.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "<strong>Observability: Seeing Problems First</strong>",
          "content": "<strong>Observability: Seeing Problems First</strong>",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "During a flash sale, millions of people are buying at once. If something breaks, you can’t wait for users to complain you need to&nbsp;<strong>spot problems instantly</strong>.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That’s why engineers watch a few&nbsp;<strong>golden signals</strong>&nbsp;on dashboards all night.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "<strong>Golden Signals (What They Watch)</strong>",
          "content": "<strong>Golden Signals (What They Watch)</strong>",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<strong>Checkout speed</strong>&nbsp;→ Every checkout should finish fast. Target: under 300 ms for almost all users.",
            "<strong>Payment success</strong>&nbsp;→ At least 95% of payments should go through. If it drops, something’s wrong with a bank or gateway.",
            "<strong>Inventory locks</strong>&nbsp;→ Reserving stock should take less than 50 ms. If it’s slow, Redis or ZooKeeper is overloaded.",
            "<strong>Kafka lag</strong>&nbsp;→ Events (orders, stock updates, payments) should be processed within 2 seconds. If delayed, stock counts and notifications may be wrong."
          ],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": [],
          "ordered": true
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "<strong>What They Do When Things Break</strong>",
          "content": "<strong>What They Do When Things Break</strong>",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "If&nbsp;<strong>Bank A fails</strong>&nbsp;→ router quickly sends less traffic to it and more to other banks.",
            "If&nbsp;<strong>Redis shard is overloaded</strong>&nbsp;→ hot product counters (like iPhone) are split across multiple Redis keys to spread the load.",
            "If&nbsp;<strong>Kafka is lagging</strong>&nbsp;→ new consumers are started, or non-critical traffic is paused, so important events catch up.",
            "Failures don’t shock the team. They&nbsp;<em>expect them</em>."
          ],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": [],
          "ordered": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "<strong>Midnight Failures</strong>",
          "content": "<strong>Midnight Failures</strong>",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<strong>12:12 AM</strong>&nbsp;→ UPI-X latency spikes. Router cuts share 30% → 2%. Wallets take over. Pending orders settle later.",
            "<strong>Hot iPhone SKU overloads Redis</strong>&nbsp;→ counter is split across 8 shards. TTL jitter avoids synchronized expiries.",
            "<strong>Kafka consumer lag</strong>&nbsp;→ engineers scale up consumers, backlog clears in minutes.",
            "<strong>Cache stampede</strong>&nbsp;→ single-flight prevents collapse."
          ],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": [],
          "ordered": false
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The system&nbsp;<em>bends but never breaks</em>.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "<em>In the weeks before Big Billion Day, engineers practice at&nbsp;<strong>3 AM</strong>&nbsp;when traffic is low. These are called&nbsp;<strong>chaos drills</strong>. They break things on purpose:</em>",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Kill a database server.",
            "Cut off a data center link.",
            "Pretend a bank goes down."
          ],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": [],
          "ordered": false
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Every time, they practice how to recover. They write down what worked, update playbooks, and fine-tune alarms. So by the time the real sale night comes,&nbsp;<strong>failures don’t surprise anyone</strong>&nbsp;they’ve already seen them in practice.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That’s why during BBD night, there’s no panic and no “hero” trying to code last-minute fixes. Instead, it’s calm and methodical. Engineers sit with dashboards open, radios on, and checklists ready.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "You’ll hear quiet voices say things like:",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<em>“Cut Bank-X traffic.”</em>",
            "<em>“Add more Kafka consumers.”</em>",
            "<em>“Turn off recommendations, keep checkout fast.”</em>"
          ],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": [],
          "ordered": false
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "And it works. By sunrise,&nbsp;<strong>crores of orders are confirmed</strong>, warehouses are buzzing, and the war room finally relaxes. Another Big Billion Sale survived.",
          "items": [],
          "leftItems": [],
          "rightItems": [],
          "cards": [],
          "metrics": [],
          "points": [],
          "layers": [],
          "exchanges": []
        },
        {
